From 94efd881634bbfc900a53f1d0ed5d41645ca142a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: abhay-byte <abhay02delhi@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 15:22:48 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] panvk/wsi: read sw frames through the uncached buffer again
 (PANVK_WSI_SW_CACHED=1 opts in)

jm-v7-wip 0115 made the sw WSI (kbase without the DRI3 dma-buf path, so
every PanPlay Wine/DXVK present) read each frame back through the cached
host memory type and invalidate it first.  The invalidate is a userland
DC CIVAC over the whole frame per present, and on the X6 Pro (MT6897, v11)
that costs more than the write-combined read it replaces:
small frames lose most (D3D11 FL 11_1 640x360: 257 fps cached, 831
uncached, rc4 803), the cube gains (255 to 271 fps, 1 % low 43 to 83),
SquidRoom D3D12 is the same (58 / 58).  rc4 (before 0115) read uncached,
which is the whole rc4 vs 115c+ fps gap on PanPlay's small-frame tests.

Default the sw readback to the uncached buffer; PANVK_WSI_SW_CACHED=1
keeps the cached read + invalidate for A/B.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_wsi.c | 13 +++++++++----
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_wsi.c b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_wsi.c
index 4d87b7ca7e2..54d35aa9667 100644
--- a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_wsi.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_wsi.c
@@ -17,6 +17,8 @@
 #include <stdlib.h>
 #include <string.h>
 
+#include "util/u_debug.h"
+
 #if defined(HAVE_PAN_KMOD_KBASE)
 #include "lib/kmod/kbase_kmod.h"
 #endif
@@ -757,12 +759,15 @@ panvk_wsi_init(struct panvk_physical_device *physical_device)
       panvk_can_present_on_device;
 
    /* The sw path reads every frame back on the CPU.  Without IO coherency
-    * the only coherent host-visible type is the uncached one, so read
-    * through the cached type and invalidate instead.
-    * PANVK_WSI_SW_CACHED=0 keeps the uncached buffer.
+    * the only coherent host-visible type is the uncached one.  Reading
+    * through the cached type needs a DC CIVAC over the whole frame before
+    * each read, and on kbase (X6 Pro, v11) that costs more than the
+    * uncached read it saves: D3D11 FL 11_1 at 640x360 257 fps cached vs
+    * 831 uncached, the cube 255 vs 271, SquidRoom equal.  So the uncached
+    * buffer is the default again; PANVK_WSI_SW_CACHED=1 reads cached.
     */
    physical_device->wsi_device.sw_cached_noncoherent =
-      PANVK_PERF(WSI_SW_CACHED);
+      debug_get_bool_option("PANVK_WSI_SW_CACHED", false);
 
    /* MIT-SHM sw present: the event thread collects each put's GetGeometry
     * reply, so the present thread copies and sends the next frame while
-- 
